      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is looking good. I think what Edward wanted to see on this was to not have an __overridable function in zork/variant_trembyle.c but instead have you define something like CONFIG_PS8818_RX_INPUT_TERM that is defaulted to undefined in config.h, and then variant_trembyle can define it for the common as PS8818_RX_INPUT_TERM_112_OHM and morphius/board.h can redefine it to be PS8818_RX_INPUT_TERM_85_OHM.  Then this function will only be defined in one location that is still used in a common manner.\n\nIt may turn out that you can start in config.h as defaulting this to PS8818_RX_INPUT_TERM_112_OHM and then you would only have to undef and then define to being 85_OHM in morphius/board.h",
